t/ext-bracken.audit.json", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01NEV7HnELjp1Gd7QZRi9P8Z"}], "text_tail": "les apply to calls before then; the JSON uses the final-release values.\n- **Missing parts of a date:** the card says to ask for them, but the schema has no value for \"ask\", so the field stays at its default.\n- **Second 1\u201314 offer:** \"Full-first still applies even to a later floor slot\" can't be fully expressed for the \"floor by deadline\" offer.\n- **Third-party rules:** \"be brief with third parties\", \"never accept their answers or promises\" and \"ask if the holder is available before a callback\" have no field in the schema.\n\nFiles are in `out/`:\n- ext-bracken.policy.json\n- ext-bracken.audit.json"}
{"event": "policy_compiled", "run_id": "c103e99cddbe4ea6adbb4f9522192187", "pid": 98611, "time": "2026-10-10T19:34:14-0700", "elapsed_s": 178.963, "artifact": "out/ext-bracken.policy.json", "bands": 2, "identity_fields": ["security_phrase", "joining_year", "contact_tail", "responsible_dob"], "special_cases": ["already_paid", "dispute", "hardship", "restructuring", "human", "scam", "refuse_to_talk", "robot", "change_saved_promise"], "unresolved": [{"topic": "calendar.missing_date_parts", "text": "Do not silently assume missing date components: ask for them. (No dedicated IR value for 'ask'; left at default.)", "doc": "sources/001-02-operating-card.md"}, {"topic": "release effective date", "text": "FINAL signed release instruction \u2014 effective 14 October. Its overrides (security order, 5 wrong answers, callbacks, 1\u201314 deadline, 2 retries, human ask-once) are applied in this policy; the documents do not say which values apply to calls before 14 October.", "doc": "sources/000-01-mail-thread.txt"}, {"topic": "bands.1-14 floor slot full-first", "text": "\"Full-first still applies even to a later floor slot.\" The second 1\u201314 slot is described as 'floor by deadline'; the documents do not say exactly how full-first is applied in that slot when full has not yet been refused (IR attempt amount set to floor as the table states).", "doc": "sources/001-02-operating-card.md"}, {"topic": "third-party conduct", "text": "Be brief with third parties; never accept their security answers or payment promises. Ask whether the named holder is available before seeking a callback. No dedicated IR field; enforced by the template's third-party flow.", "doc": "sources/001-02-operating-card.md"}], "audit_fixed": ["special_cases[scam].before_persuasion false -> true: the card lists it under '## Exceptions (before any collection persuasion)'.", "special_cases[refuse_to_talk].before_persuasion false -> true: same 'Exceptions (before any collection persuasion)' heading.", "Enriched several source spans (callback outcomes, band 1-14 offer text, confirm phrase, dob no-hint text) so each value cites its supporting sentence.", "Added unresolved entries for the 'Full-first still applies even to a later floor slot' nuance and for third-party conduct rules that have no IR field."], "audit_unresolved": ["Missing date components must be asked for; the IR has no explicit 'ask' value (missing_date_parts left at default 'unresolved').", "The final release is 'effective 14 October' (today is 2026-10-11); the documents do not say which values govern calls before that date. The final-release values are applied.", "How 'Full-first still applies even to a later floor slot' interacts with the 1\u201314 'floor by deadline' slot is not fully expressible in the attempt DSL.", "Third-party brevity / never accept third-party answers or promises / ask holder availability before callback have no dedicated IR field."], "defaulted_without_source": []}
